<i>The things you can do are so striking</i>

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:05.050
"Carve Them In! The Scars of Destiny"

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:05.010
In this era of globalization,

00:03:05.010 --> 00:03:09.180
the internet has become an indispensable tool.

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:08.550
"1993 A.D."

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:13.890
I declare that, in the future, communication between people

00:03:13.890 --> 00:03:17.760
will become impossible without the internet.

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:19.390
This technology,

00:03:19.390 --> 00:03:23.030
which instantly connects even people separated by great distances,

00:03:23.030 --> 00:03:25.700
is the great invention

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:27.860
which will advance us to the next stage.

00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:34.210
Twenty-two years ago, with Mao Hayashi as CEO,

00:03:34.210 --> 00:03:37.610
and the technical adviser
Sougon Kenzaki at its center,

00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:42.580
Japan's first network management company, Nesta, was established.

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:46.590
"Tokyo Financial Times

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:46.590
A first domestically! Network Management

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:46.590
Company Nesta Launches"

00:03:42.580 --> 00:03:46.550
By bringing the internet, now an aspect of everyday life, to this country,

00:03:46.550 --> 00:03:48.560
and developing it,

00:03:46.590 --> 00:03:50.090
"The Key to Nesta's Rapid Growth"

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:52.720
Nesta succeeded in rapidly expanding its business.

00:03:57.430 --> 00:03:59.270
It's been five years since we started the business,

00:03:59.270 --> 00:04:03.400
and in that time, Nesta has grown into one of the world's leading companies.

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:05.440
It has all gone as you anticipated.

00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:10.410
It's thanks to your ability to explain the importance of the network.

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:12.580
I couldn't have done that so well on my own.

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:16.080
It really was the right choice to have you be company president.

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:18.290
Everything starts from here.

00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:20.120
Through the development of the network,

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:22.290
the density of communication will increase,

00:04:22.290 --> 00:04:24.930
which will ultimately bring your dream to fruition.

00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:28.630
Your dream to recreate the world of truth.

00:04:28.630 --> 00:04:30.600
Until 12,000 years ago,

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:34.640
the world of truth existed directly adjacent to our own.

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:39.610
By touching it, people could make the rain fall by wishing for it,

00:04:39.610 --> 00:04:42.780
and could summon a typhoon by wishing for wind.

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:47.650
Basically, it was the power to materialize what people thought or felt.

00:04:47.650 --> 00:04:51.620
People's wishes called the phenomenon into being from the truth.

00:04:51.620 --> 00:04:53.320
Like magic.

00:04:53.320 --> 00:04:56.660
The baby that could be called the key to materializing that dream-like world

00:04:56.660 --> 00:05:00.120
will be born tomorrow.

00:05:01.130 --> 00:05:03.030
Do you honestly believe in that?

00:05:03.030 --> 00:05:06.170
Do you believe in the one chosen by Verbalism?

00:05:06.170 --> 00:05:09.300
Trying to jump straight to results through a miracle...

00:05:09.300 --> 00:05:11.470
I'm not fond of the idea.

00:05:11.470 --> 00:05:16.310
If communication develops, the world of truth will eventually appear.

00:05:16.310 --> 00:05:17.650
Is that not enough?

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:21.180
The development of communication and the coming of a chosen one.

00:05:21.180 --> 00:05:24.890
My interpretation is that both will be necessary.

00:05:24.890 --> 00:05:27.660
You... don't understand.

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:28.990
What do you mean?

00:05:28.990 --> 00:05:31.890
Having your fate determined for you before you're born...

00:05:31.890 --> 00:05:34.260
That is a very sad thing.

00:05:36.830 --> 00:05:39.570
I see. Mao said that, did she?

00:05:39.570 --> 00:05:42.170
She's very human.

00:05:42.170 --> 00:05:45.370
Well, too bad her brother's such an inhuman monster, huh?

00:05:47.210 --> 00:05:50.880
Normally, I couldn't tell you about this,

00:05:50.880 --> 00:05:56.680
but a baby boy was born at precisely the time you said.

00:05:56.680 --> 00:06:00.020
From what we were told, soon after giving birth,

00:06:00.020 --> 00:06:03.890
the baby's mother passed away, and the child had no other relatives.

00:06:03.890 --> 00:06:08.400
It felt like everything was agreeing with fate.

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:12.060
Subete. That will be this boy's name.

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:19.040
Because this boy lost everything at birth.

00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:21.910
But you know, not having anything

00:06:21.910 --> 00:06:25.210
means that everything is there for him to gain.

00:06:26.280 --> 00:06:28.620
Over the course of this child's life,

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:30.950
he will gain everything.

00:06:30.950 --> 00:06:33.420
He will live freely, by his own will,

00:06:33.420 --> 00:06:36.420
and take hold of love, dreams, and everything else.

00:06:36.420 --> 00:06:38.450
So, I named him Subete--"everything."

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:41.960
I see.

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:43.770
Even after they took in Subete,

00:06:43.770 --> 00:06:47.070
Sougon never married Mao.

00:06:47.070 --> 00:06:52.110
Sougon saw Subete as a tool to reach the world of truth.

00:06:52.110 --> 00:06:56.610
And Mao wanted him to live freely as a human being.

00:06:56.610 --> 00:06:58.750
The difference in their views

00:06:58.750 --> 00:07:03.750
may have created an invisible wall between them.

00:07:03.750 --> 00:07:08.420
Eventually, Sougon and I delegated all of Nesta's management to Mao,

00:07:08.420 --> 00:07:12.330
heading overseas to excavate and study ruins.

00:07:12.330 --> 00:07:15.600
We needed to deepen our understanding of written culture,

00:07:15.600 --> 00:07:20.260
or we wouldn't understand how to recreate the world of truth.

00:07:22.100 --> 00:07:26.270
Dear Mao. Are you and Subete doing well?

00:07:26.270 --> 00:07:28.610
I'm getting by fine over here.

00:07:28.610 --> 00:07:30.450
What we recently excavated

00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:34.150
was a relic from the ancient writing culture, as I thought.

00:07:34.150 --> 00:07:36.320
If we succeed in deciphering their script,

00:07:36.320 --> 00:07:39.290
it should be a useful resource for our research.

00:07:39.290 --> 00:07:41.190
I'd like to hear your voice.

00:07:41.190 --> 00:07:44.630
I hope you'll answer your phone when you have time.

00:07:44.630 --> 00:07:45.830
Good morning.

00:07:45.830 --> 00:07:48.130
We're both busy, and there's the time zone difference to consider,

00:07:48.130 --> 00:07:51.330
so e-mail probably works best for both of us.

00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:55.500
"Good morning. We're both busy, and there's

00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:55.500
the time zone difference to consider,

00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:55.500
so e-mail probably works best for both of us.

00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:55.500
I am doing well. Work is hectic, but I'm

00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:55.500
giving it my best. I'm holding up fine,

00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:55.500
so don't worry about me."

00:07:51.330 --> 00:07:53.030
I am doing well.

00:07:53.030 --> 00:07:55.970
Work is hectic, but I'm giving it my best.

00:07:55.970 --> 00:07:58.540
I'm holding up fine, so don't worry about me.

00:07:58.540 --> 00:08:00.640
I'm glad to hear you're well.

00:08:00.640 --> 00:08:03.140
I'm not worried about the company.

00:08:03.140 --> 00:08:06.310
I know you'll do a great job.

00:08:13.520 --> 00:08:15.150
Come over here!

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:23.000
Written material? Is it a book?

00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:26.000
We found this here.

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:28.340
Sorry for the late reply.

00:08:28.340 --> 00:08:32.870
I have a lot of complicated work to do, so it's been hard to find time.

00:08:32.870 --> 00:08:36.940
Don't worry about me. I'm fine.

00:08:36.440 --> 00:08:37.910
"Sorry for the late reply. I have a lot of

00:08:36.440 --> 00:08:37.910
complicated work to do, so it's been hard

00:08:36.440 --> 00:08:37.910
to find time. Don't worry about me. I'm fine."

00:08:41.680 --> 00:08:44.920
Well, have you managed to decipher the stone book?

00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:46.390
No.

00:08:46.390 --> 00:08:48.520
But there's a whole book written here.

00:08:48.520 --> 00:08:52.590
Whatever is written in it must be important...

00:08:52.590 --> 00:08:55.360
It's been almost two years now since we left Japan.

00:08:55.360 --> 00:08:58.700
You must be missing your family by now.

00:08:58.700 --> 00:09:01.290
Mao may have been right.

00:09:02.540 --> 00:09:04.770
There was no need to rush things.

00:09:04.770 --> 00:09:07.210
We don't need to tie this child down with fate.

00:09:07.210 --> 00:09:12.050
With the power of the network, the world will eventually reach the truth.

00:09:12.050 --> 00:09:16.550
I don't know how many years it'll take, but I'm certain it will happen.

00:09:16.550 --> 00:09:19.090
I see.

00:09:19.090 --> 00:09:21.560
Mr. Kenzaki, President Hayashi has...!

00:09:21.560 --> 00:09:23.050
What is it?

00:09:35.240 --> 00:09:38.970
When she was driving fast, trying to lose a journalist,

00:09:38.970 --> 00:09:42.910
she lost control and collided with a noise barrier.

00:09:42.480 --> 00:09:43.980
"Weekly Truth

00:09:42.480 --> 00:09:43.980
The Darkness of Nesta"

00:09:43.980 --> 00:09:46.950
"Biggest in the industry! The Darkness of Nesta

00:09:43.980 --> 00:09:46.950
Starting a lewd new business using

00:09:43.980 --> 00:09:46.950
every weapon in her womanly arsenal!

00:09:43.980 --> 00:09:46.950
The woman who slept with the network!"

00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:49.920
What is this?

00:09:49.920 --> 00:09:52.590
The country had its eye on Nesta's rapid growth,

00:09:52.590 --> 00:09:56.820
and they want to nationalize our network business.

00:09:56.820 --> 00:10:00.490
But that's only in name.
It's basically a takeover.

00:10:00.490 --> 00:10:03.430
Ever since you left the country,

00:10:03.430 --> 00:10:06.000
they've been waiting for an opportunity.

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:08.440
The president absolutely refused to give in.

00:10:08.440 --> 00:10:13.170
And so, they began to bash her in the most foul of ways, using the media.

00:10:13.170 --> 00:10:15.510
That left her feeling cornered.

00:10:15.510 --> 00:10:19.280
The reason she lost control of her vehicle may well have been...

00:10:19.280 --> 00:10:21.450
Why did you never tell me?!

00:10:21.450 --> 00:10:23.650
The president ordered me not to.

00:10:23.650 --> 00:10:26.520
She said she didn't want to get in your way.

00:10:28.660 --> 00:10:34.300
Subete was miraculously unharmed, despite being in the same car.

00:10:34.300 --> 00:10:38.230
She must have given her life to protect him.

00:10:57.820 --> 00:11:00.720
How is this... communication?

00:11:00.720 --> 00:11:03.320
How is it a bond between people?

00:11:10.200 --> 00:11:12.600
"Anon 874: **sta is finished.

00:11:10.200 --> 00:11:12.600
Anon 875: Money obsessed ghouls.

00:11:10.200 --> 00:11:12.600
Anon 876: Go dye! Er, I mean die!!

00:11:10.200 --> 00:11:12.600
Anon 877: They're total scum.

00:11:10.200 --> 00:11:12.600
Anon 878: Someone kill her."

00:11:14.600 --> 00:11:16.870
"But I'm trying my hardest. I'm fine."

00:11:17.840 --> 00:11:20.710
I didn't understand anything...

00:11:20.710 --> 00:11:23.180
Not one thing.

00:11:29.520 --> 00:11:31.220
I reject it!

00:11:31.220 --> 00:11:34.090
The development of modern written civilization,

00:11:34.090 --> 00:11:36.760
which so easily tramples on the feelings of others.

00:11:36.760 --> 00:11:38.190
I will not forgive it.

00:11:38.190 --> 00:11:42.030
This is a society infested with writing and devoid of heart.

00:11:42.030 --> 00:11:45.090
And so, I must destroy it.

00:11:58.380 --> 00:12:01.910
The power of truth is in your hands.

00:12:07.720 --> 00:12:09.490
What is this?

00:12:11.560 --> 00:12:14.550
I understand now. So that's how it was.

00:12:17.300 --> 00:12:20.400
When he took hold of the Book of Verbalism,

00:12:20.400 --> 00:12:24.110
all sorts of knowledge must have flowed into him.

00:12:24.110 --> 00:12:26.240
The destruction of modern civilization.

00:12:26.240 --> 00:12:30.230
Only through that sacrifice can the world of truth appear.

00:12:40.490 --> 00:12:41.980
Do not cry.

00:12:43.120 --> 00:12:47.490
You are the chosen one who will change this world.

00:13:07.680 --> 00:13:10.020
My father's recognition...

00:13:10.020 --> 00:13:12.610
That was everything to me back then.

00:13:14.460 --> 00:13:16.550
Dad! Wait!

00:13:20.030 --> 00:13:23.460
I had... no mother.

00:13:23.460 --> 00:13:25.630
I only had my father.

00:13:25.630 --> 00:13:29.040
Yet my father wouldn't even look at me.

00:13:29.040 --> 00:13:31.640
It's not because you've done anything wrong.

00:13:31.640 --> 00:13:34.810
But still, when he looks at your face,

00:13:34.810 --> 00:13:38.650
it brings back painful memories for him.

00:13:38.650 --> 00:13:40.140
Want some?

00:13:45.520 --> 00:13:48.320
I couldn't really understand...

00:13:48.320 --> 00:13:50.720
...what Mr. Hayashi was trying to tell me.

00:13:52.660 --> 00:13:54.330
I was desperate.

00:13:54.330 --> 00:13:56.360
If I did as Dad said,

00:13:56.360 --> 00:13:59.870
I believed he would look my way someday.

00:13:59.870 --> 00:14:01.500
No success today either, huh?

00:14:01.500 --> 00:14:03.500
That's it for this attempt.

00:14:03.500 --> 00:14:06.270
Get to work taking down and recalibrating the equipment.

00:14:11.410 --> 00:14:15.020
Dad! Did you come here to see me?

00:14:15.020 --> 00:14:18.590
You were not chosen.

00:14:18.590 --> 00:14:21.260
You are a failure.

00:14:21.260 --> 00:14:22.860
I have found replacements.

00:14:22.860 --> 00:14:26.030
I will create someone compatible from among them.

00:14:26.030 --> 00:14:28.260
I no longer need you.

00:14:30.760 --> 00:14:32.900
Far away...

00:14:32.900 --> 00:14:37.240
It felt like he was going far away, beyond where I could reach him.

00:14:37.240 --> 00:14:39.540
You're wrong!

00:14:39.540 --> 00:14:40.880
I can do it!

00:14:40.880 --> 00:14:44.570
For I am... the chosen one!

00:14:50.420 --> 00:14:53.050
This is...

00:14:53.050 --> 00:14:55.250
It's coming! We've succeeded!

00:14:59.390 --> 00:15:01.920
I thought this would make him recognize me.

00:15:03.600 --> 00:15:05.770
But...

00:15:05.770 --> 00:15:06.970
...even after that,

00:15:06.970 --> 00:15:11.410
my father never looked at me... not even once.

00:15:28.760 --> 00:15:30.250
Dad!

00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:38.160
Protect us.

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:45.340
You don't have the Book of Verbalism. How?

00:15:45.340 --> 00:15:47.980
I have no need of that thing.

00:15:47.980 --> 00:15:52.510
For you... are the chosen one.

00:15:52.510 --> 00:15:55.780
Oh, come on! Isn't it a bit late to be saying that?

00:15:55.780 --> 00:15:59.520
You said Akira Kaibuki was the chosen one!

00:15:59.520 --> 00:16:04.630
Until you're on your last chance, you can't show your power.

00:16:04.630 --> 00:16:06.690
It's the same bad habit you've always had.

00:16:06.690 --> 00:16:08.160
That's...

00:16:08.160 --> 00:16:09.650
Go!

00:16:10.700 --> 00:16:13.470
Wait, Dad! What about you?

00:16:13.470 --> 00:16:17.200
Let me go. To where she is...

00:16:17.200 --> 00:16:21.310
What are you saying? I don't understand, Dad!

00:16:21.310 --> 00:16:24.640
Dad!

00:16:41.200 --> 00:16:42.700
Hey.

00:16:42.700 --> 00:16:45.530
You're quite the late sleeper.

00:16:45.530 --> 00:16:47.330
Mr. Hayashi?

00:16:47.330 --> 00:16:51.210
You just suddenly dropped on the ground in front of me.

00:16:51.210 --> 00:16:56.200
I have no clue how you made it back from the Logos World.

00:16:57.880 --> 00:17:00.010
Mr. Hayashi...

00:17:00.010 --> 00:17:02.250
Dad is...

00:17:02.250 --> 00:17:04.020
Why?

00:17:04.020 --> 00:17:07.010
Can you stand? Come with me.

00:17:09.060 --> 00:17:14.230
You were still young, so you may not remember.

00:17:14.230 --> 00:17:15.860
This way.

00:17:20.030 --> 00:17:21.090
"Mao Hayashi

00:17:20.030 --> 00:17:21.090
1969-2000"

00:17:22.400 --> 00:17:24.030
"September 10th

00:17:22.400 --> 00:17:24.030
Sougon Kenzaki"

00:17:27.780 --> 00:17:29.640
"September 10th

00:17:27.780 --> 00:17:29.640
Sougon Kenzaki"

00:17:28.040 --> 00:17:30.380
Dad?

00:17:30.380 --> 00:17:33.210
Every time your birthday came,

00:17:33.210 --> 00:17:37.550
he would come here to leave a letter.
He did it this year as well, of course.

00:17:42.790 --> 00:17:44.390
Dear Mao.

00:17:44.390 --> 00:17:46.890
This day of the year has come around again.

00:17:46.890 --> 00:17:50.100
Subete has turned 17 now.

00:17:50.100 --> 00:17:52.460
He's grown to be a fine young man.

00:17:55.400 --> 00:17:59.070
But, today, I have something
I must apologize to you for.

00:17:59.070 --> 00:18:01.810
I lied to that boy.

00:18:01.810 --> 00:18:03.640
What is this power?

00:18:03.640 --> 00:18:06.740
We'll pound through it, with our fists!

00:18:08.420 --> 00:18:13.420
In order to stimulate Subete's growth and bring out his true power,

00:18:11.320 --> 00:18:12.650
"Fist"

00:18:13.420 --> 00:18:15.460
I told him that the enemy he confronts

00:18:15.460 --> 00:18:19.090
is the chosen one.

00:18:21.160 --> 00:18:22.960
"Mugen Punch"

00:18:22.830 --> 00:18:24.800
Mugen Punch!

00:18:27.430 --> 00:18:31.170
I believe that boy will become strong.

00:18:31.170 --> 00:18:35.980
But, at the same time, I have realized my own misgivings.

00:18:35.980 --> 00:18:38.110
Mao, you said it yourself.

00:18:38.110 --> 00:18:40.780
You wanted the boy to live freely.

00:18:40.780 --> 00:18:44.520
You wanted him to grasp his love and his dreams by his own will.

00:18:44.520 --> 00:18:48.160
If Subete denies his own fate,

00:18:48.160 --> 00:18:52.530
that boy may be able to live freely by his own will.

00:18:52.530 --> 00:18:56.000
I would like to see him walk that path in life, as well.

00:18:56.000 --> 00:18:59.170
I now think that, despite everything.

00:18:59.170 --> 00:19:01.400
That's why, back then...

00:19:26.230 --> 00:19:28.230
High energy readings!

00:19:28.230 --> 00:19:30.900
What is going on?
These readings aren't normal!

00:19:30.900 --> 00:19:34.160
This isn't ordinary Verbalism Ability. It's...

00:19:35.400 --> 00:19:37.170
The Book of Verbalism?!

00:19:37.170 --> 00:19:38.830
Akira Kaibuki.

00:19:40.040 --> 00:19:43.880
I can hear a voice. But our comms aren't supposed to be working.

00:19:43.880 --> 00:19:46.180
You called yourself a savior, didn't you?

00:19:46.180 --> 00:19:49.680
I understand everything there is to know about your voice now.

00:19:49.680 --> 00:19:54.090
"Savior." That word is your raison d'être.

00:19:54.090 --> 00:19:58.090
That is why you were looking for me.

00:19:58.090 --> 00:20:00.560
A savior is one who saves others.

00:20:00.560 --> 00:20:02.900
For you to be yourself,

00:20:02.900 --> 00:20:06.530
there must always be another threatening the world.

00:20:06.530 --> 00:20:08.570
--Shut up.
--Accept it.

00:20:08.570 --> 00:20:11.870
You desire a threat to the world.

00:20:11.870 --> 00:20:13.360
Akira.

00:20:17.440 --> 00:20:18.540
"Sun Mugen Punch"

00:20:20.480 --> 00:20:21.640
"Sun Mugen Punch"

00:20:22.050 --> 00:20:23.720
Scorch!

00:20:23.720 --> 00:20:25.780
Sun Mugen Punch!

00:20:27.720 --> 00:20:29.620
Rejoice, Akira.

00:20:29.620 --> 00:20:34.760
Your wish... I will grant it for you.

00:20:34.760 --> 00:20:38.300
Wishes are the one thing people can't leave behind.

00:20:38.300 --> 00:20:44.610
The wishes of the departed are washed away with their lives and vanish.

00:20:44.610 --> 00:20:48.310
Yet still, you'll live on.

00:20:48.310 --> 00:20:50.970
Even though I've lost everything.

00:20:53.580 --> 00:20:55.570
No, that's wrong.

00:20:57.580 --> 00:20:59.950
I still have my pain.

00:20:59.950 --> 00:21:02.090
This pain is the one thing I have!

00:21:02.090 --> 00:21:04.960
Over the course of this child's life,

00:21:04.960 --> 00:21:07.430
he will gain everything.

00:21:07.430 --> 00:21:10.260
He will live freely, by his own will,

00:21:10.260 --> 00:21:13.790
and take hold of love, dreams, and everything else.

00:21:15.470 --> 00:21:20.100
This is my will. It is...

00:21:22.780 --> 00:21:25.840
Defeating you is everything to me.

00:21:30.120 --> 00:21:31.640
The Mugen Punch...!

00:21:35.990 --> 00:21:37.720
I'll be taking that.

00:21:41.800 --> 00:21:43.290
Akira!

00:21:45.130 --> 00:21:46.620
Subete!

00:21:54.170 --> 00:21:55.010
"Mugen Everything to Ashes Sword"

00:21:55.380 --> 00:21:58.140
Reduce everything to ashes.

00:22:00.510 --> 00:22:01.640
"Mugen Everything to Ashes Sword"

00:22:16.200 --> 00:22:18.500
I will destroy.

00:22:18.500 --> 00:22:20.560
Because you save.

00:22:37.420 --> 00:22:40.890
<i>Je-Je t'aime communication</i>

00:22:40.890 --> 00:22:50.890
<i>Oh, you aren't making a bit of</i> <i>eye contact with me while you talk</i>

00:22:50.930 --> 00:23:00.140
<i>Are you texting some far-off</i> <i>neighboring world or something?</i>

00:23:00.140 --> 00:23:05.270
<i>Because this isn't communication at all</i>

00:23:07.210 --> 00:23:13.750
<i>You'd at least understand that much</i>

00:23:13.750 --> 00:23:19.760
<i>even if the times suddenly changed, right?</i>

00:23:19.760 --> 00:23:23.760
<i>Give me je t'aime communication sometimes</i>

00:23:23.760 --> 00:23:27.170
<i>Look at me, answer me, and tell me</i>

00:23:27.170 --> 00:23:33.670
<i>I mean, this is practically</i> <i>like talking to a computer</i>

00:23:33.670 --> 00:23:36.680
<i>A-Adieu application</i>

00:23:36.680 --> 00:23:43.320
<i>Even if it means staying lonely</i> <i>in my heart, if it'll connect us</i>

00:23:43.320 --> 00:23:49.690
<i>then, please, at least show</i> <i>your smile to me alone</i>

00:23:51.790 --> 00:23:53.330
Why is Subete here?

00:23:53.330 --> 00:23:55.000
Maia, you were fabulous again today!

00:23:55.000 --> 00:23:56.260
No, I was no different from usual.

00:23:56.260 --> 00:23:58.670
No, you were definitely cute! Right, Akira?

00:23:58.670 --> 00:24:01.330
Gross. I don't recall allowing you to call me by name.

00:24:01.330 --> 00:24:04.840
Also, you said earlier that Kokone
Kikogami and Karan Uminagi are cute.

00:24:04.840 --> 00:24:06.270
--Eep.
--He's an enemy, all right.

00:24:06.270 --> 00:24:08.510
--He's an enemy.
--N-Next time, Episode 17.

00:24:07.310 --> 00:24:09.840
"Episode 17: Shatter!

00:24:07.310 --> 00:24:09.840
The One I Must Strike Down"

00:24:08.510 --> 00:24:09.780
"Shatter! The One I Must Strike Down."

00:24:09.780 --> 00:24:10.940
Don't come back.
